mmi: R5900 lane layouts for the multiply, divide, permute and variable-shift
MMI instructions (ps2_mmi.h). PMULTH/PMADDH/PMSUBH/PHMADH/PHMSBH and the word
multiplies summed every lane into one 64-bit value; PDIVW/PDIVUW/PDIVBW
divided one lane and wrote rd; PEXEW, PEXCW, PROT3W, PEXEH, PEXCH, PREVH,
PINTH and PINTEH used the wrong shuffles; PSLLVW/PSRLVW/PSRAVW shifted rs by rt
per word instead of rt by rs on words 0 and 2 with sign extension. KH2's effect
code uses PROT3W, PEXEW, PMADDH + PMFHL.SH and PDIVW.

